WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.501
-Congrats on the album,
"Takin' It Back."

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.300
-Thank you.
-We have lots to talk about.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.801
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.334
I'm just -- It's not every day

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:10.934
you're on the show
with T. Swift, bro.

00:00:10.934 --> 00:00:12.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.567
-Stop, come on.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.133
You guys must know each other,
right?

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.167
-Just briefly.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:18.501
-Now you're British
all of a sudden, too?

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.701
-Briefly.
-"Briefly."

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.400
-Oh, my God, it's the nerves.
-It's the nerves.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.300
-Okay, I'm here.
-Last time I saw you was

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.767
when we played "Password"
together, wasn't it?

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:27.067
-Yes.
-You were very --

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.167
-Yes!
-"Yes!"

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.334
-I was very aggressive then too.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:30.901
-You were very competitive
and very funny.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:32.100
-Yes. Oh, thank you.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.234
-And then you ended up almost --
-Winning.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.133
-Yeah, and destroying me
at the end.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.868
You got in there by the end.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.968
But there was one word that you
didn't get that made me laugh.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.367
-Oh, we're going to bring
this up?

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.267
[ Laughter ]
-Well, I mean, it just --

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.767
It was starting to
trend on Twitter.

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:45.868
So, I was like, "Oh, yeah."

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.567
You didn't know
what manscaping was.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:48.968
-Listen!
-Yeah.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:51.467
[ Laughter ]
-Do you know what manscaping is?

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.033
-Yeah.
[ Audience says "yes" ]

00:00:53.033 --> 00:00:54.767
-Whatever.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.734
-Yeah. Everyone's like, "Yeah."

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.567
But, yeah, that was interesting,
you never -- you're like --

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:00.601
-I --
-Yeah, you're like --

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:02.400
-Mama never taught me
what that really meant.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.434
-"Mama never taught me."

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.234
-My mom's here tonight
and my dad.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.767
-Hey, we love you, Mom and Dad.
You gotta be proud.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.701 --> 00:01:13.400
Ah, there they are.
Hey, Dad, come on.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.701
There's your dad. Come on.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.334
You gotta be very proud.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:20.968
Is he a happy grandpa?
-Shoulders back.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:23.267
-Happy grandpa too?
-Grandpa?

00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:25.501
-Yeah. Well, I mean --
Well, you got a baby.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:27.601
-Huh?
Oh, oh, he's a grandpa now.

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:28.968
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:32.067
-I was like -- I was like,
"Auntie Flo is here,

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.200
but I don't know if my grandpa
is here."

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.601
I thought you were
surprising me.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.934
-Your dad is a grandpa. Yes.
-My father is a grandfather.

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.801
-Your father is a grandfather.
-I have a baby!

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:40.968
-Yes! How is baby, then?
-Yes. He's perfect.

00:01:40.968 --> 00:01:42.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.934
-He's perfect?
-He's perfect.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.634
I just dragged him all over
Australia and now here

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:50.000
and he finally at the end of
the trip says, "Mama,"

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.801
which is great.
-Oh, it's the best in the world.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.634
-Right? He did say "dada" first.
Thank you for your kids book.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.767
He has kids books.
-Yeah, thank you. Yeah.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.968
I was asking -- I was like,
"What music is he into?"

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:00.400
Because sometimes, the kids'
music are like,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.200
"Is it baby shark?
Is it this theme?"

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.100
-I saw Saucy Santana.
-Yes.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:08.667
-Singing "Booty" on here.
-Yes.

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:10.934
-And that's my son's
favorite song.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:13.167
-Booty, booty, booty, booty,
booty, booty, booty, booty.

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.367
-Every time we get him out of
the bathtub to, like, dry him

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:16.834
off, we're like,
"Yeah, I know you like

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:19.267
my booty, booty, booty, booty."
And he cracks up.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.801
He watches the music video
every night to go to sleep.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.367
-He's so cute.

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:24.200
Can we talk about
"Takin' It Back"?

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.501
-Okay.
-Congratulations.

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:30.334
-Thank you.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:32.267
-What inspired
the album title here?

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.767
-Oh, all my albums start with T
for Trainor,

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:38.267
my family represent.
-That's right.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:41.000
-When I started writing this
album, a co-writer said,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.868
"You know, I had some artists
coming in here saying,

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.133
'I want to do
the Meghan Trainor sound.'"

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:45.467
And I was like,
"You mean the doo-wop?"

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.667
And then on TikTok,
title was blowing up.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.501
And I was like, "The universe is
speaking and I am listening."

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:53.367
So I wanted to take it back
to doo-wop times.

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:55.434
-So you listened to the fans.
You're like, "Yeah, you want it?

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:56.734
I'll give it to you."
-Yeah. Give what you want.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:58.501
-Yes.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:01.167
You worked with an incredible
producer on this album.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:03.300
In fact, we have a clip.
Here's Meghan in the studio

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.868
with her producer, who happens
to be a 1-year-old.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:07.234
Take a look.
-Oh.

00:03:07.234 --> 00:03:08.267
♪♪

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:13.167
[ Audience aws ]

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:14.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:18.100
You just -- You just kiss him
and hold him all day long?

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.367
-Yeah, I snuggle him.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:21.601
-Yeah, that's what
you have to do.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.534
-You have to.
-Did becoming a mom change

00:03:24.534 --> 00:03:26.000
how you write some of the songs
on your new album?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.634
-Oh, yeah.
I'm, like, way better.

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:28.934
You know what I mean? I just --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.667
Well, everything is
way more important. You know?

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:31.968
I have, like,
a big fear of death,

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.634
and now it's just times
a thousand.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.934
But I'm like, "Everything means
so much more."

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:37.334
And you can hear that
in my lyrics.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.534
-Yeah.
-It's not sad. It's happy.

00:03:39.534 --> 00:03:42.634
-No, this is a happy, happy,
happy record.

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:46.567
I'm trying to think about here
which one is my favorite jam.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.501
-You listened?

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:49.567
-Yes, of course I did.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.200
In fact, I saw the video,
by the way,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:54.801
in Times Square
on a giant billboard.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.534
-You go to Times Square?
-Of course.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.234
I always go to
Bubba Gump Shrimp.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:00.701
I go, "Hey, what's up,
everybody?"

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:02.701
-Oh, love it.
-Of course. Absolutely.

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:05.300
You're performing a song for us
after the break.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.300
-"Made you look."
-Is it -- Yes.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's the video I love,

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:11.300
"Made You Look."

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.467
When you do a new song,
do you -- when you perform --

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.767
-It's terrifying.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:15.901
-It is?
-Yes.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.234
-I was going to say,
do you get nervous?

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:19.000
-[ Scottish accent ]
I'm shakin' in my boots.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:22.300
Don't ask me what that was.
-"Shaking in my boots"?

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.801
Now you're a Scot?
"I'm shakin' in my boots."

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.534
-But also,
it's a T. Swift night,

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:27.367
so everyone is gonna watch this!
-Yes!

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.601
-So, I'm like --

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.767
-Yes, Taylor is watching this
as well.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.133
-No, she's not!
-Yes, she is!

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:33.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.434
But don't you --
You can't be nervous.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.434
You're Meghan Trainor.
-I'm so nervous!

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.367
I fall on this stage.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.133
It's where I'm triggered
because I fell here.

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.400
-You fell once here.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.434
-I did fall once,
and you laid with me.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.467
And I thank you for that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.400
I'll never forget that.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.200
-Remember that?
-Yeah.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.501
-Remember that?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.501 --> 00:04:54.701
Remember?
-No, no.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:55.968
-I remember because --
-Remember her shame?

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:57.834
-No, because you're
the greatest because I go --

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.834
You're doing this whole thing
and then you're dancing

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.133
as well as singing,
which you don't --

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:04.100
-That's hard to do.
-No, you're very talented.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.534
But then that last move happened
and you were on heels

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:09.467
and you fell and then I went
over and laid down next to you

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.100
and go, "We'll be right back
with more 'Tonight Show.'"

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.934
-Yeah.
-But then I go, "Do you want --

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:14.234
Let's do it again if you want to
do it again.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.334
No problem.
Don't worry about it."

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:16.934
And you go,
"No, that really happened.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.300
I'm not afraid of that.
I'm not ashamed.

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.000
Let's show everyone
what happened."

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.000
And that's why we love you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.234
That's why we love you.

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:26.000
-I'm real.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.868
-You're performing the song

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:29.200
from "Takin' It Back"
after the break.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.467
Meghan Trainor, everyone.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:34.300
"Made You Look"
when we come back.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.801
More "Tonight Show."

